// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Marta Kowalski's triplex at 418 Alder St, Rochester NY, 2026-01-01 .. 2026-06-30. She lives in unit A and rents B and C
// through a property manager at 8%. Tenants with deposits, repairs against improvements, depreciation per part, and a
// vacancy: unit C is empty from 03-21 to 05-14.
//
// Written against PROPOSAL §6 and ASSOCIATIONS.md. After examples/explore-v5/03-triplex, whose units had to be owners so
// that a share could be borne by them. Here a unit is a part of the building with an area, a lease is a relator, and
// nobody is invented.
//
//   ✗ cannot say     ✎ says it badly     ? unclear     ⇄ what sync would need     ▸ derived, never typed
// Ids: ll-c02 is landlord, c = cannot say, 02; [A12] is the change in REPORT.md that closes it.
// Numbers: the mortgage is the ACTUS annuity (374,400 at 5.25% over 30 years, 2,067.45, first payment 2022-10-01,
// 39 payments made by 12-31); depreciation is 27.5 years straight line, mid-month; every balance is a replay.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

base USD
use us/ny
use us/rental

/// Marta, a nurse practitioner. Her pay is outside this book's interest: a net amount lands on the last day.
entity marta : person
  born    1979-05-30
  filing  single
  lives   us/ny

entity elena, devon, jordan-lee : person      // tenants. Nothing about them says so: the lease does, on the days it runs  [A12]

// ── the building and its parts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// 3,200 sqft. Bought 2022-08-12 for 468,000.00, 62,000.00 of it land. The kind `building` has a many-slot, `parts`, whose
/// weights are the parts' own `area`: the price, the land, the interest, the tax and every bill of the whole are divided by
/// them. The v4 file made each unit an owner of a rental-business to carry the percentages by hand.
asset triplex : building
  owner marta
  land  62_000 USD
  unit-a : home           area 1_150 SQFT              // marta's own: personal use, never depreciated
  unit-b : rental-home    area 1_050 SQFT  in-service 2022-09-01
  unit-c : rental-home    area 1_000 SQFT  in-service 2022-09-01

// ── the manager, and the money it holds ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

entity elm-pm : property-manager
  marta/trust : trust-account               // custody: marta's money and her tenants' deposits, with the manager; `pays out monthly on 10`
    pays out monthly on 10 all before the 1st   // ✗ ll-c05 [A6]

/// Elm keeps 8% of rent and half a month's rent for placing a tenant. `scope` is a many-slot of the agreement; a lease picks
/// its agent from whichever agreement has its unit in scope.
contract elm-agreement : management
  owner marta
  manager elm-pm
  scope unit-b, unit-c
  fee 8% of rent #management
  leasing 50% of a month's rent when a lease starts #leasing-fee

// ── leases: a relator among tenant, unit, landlord and agent ───────────────────────────────────────

contract lease-b : lease
  tenant elena                              // landlord = unit-b's owner (marta); agent = elm-pm; both by default
  unit unit-b
  1_850.00 USD monthly on 1 into trust #rent of unit
  deposit 1_850.00 USD                      // held by the agent, in the trust, tied for elena
  from 2025-07-01 until 2026-06-30
contract lease-c : lease
  tenant devon
  unit unit-c
  1_950.00 USD monthly on 1 into trust #rent of unit
  deposit 1_950.00 USD
  from 2025-09-01 until 2026-08-31
contract lease-c2 : lease
  tenant jordan-lee
  unit unit-c
  2_050.00 USD monthly on 1 into trust #rent of unit prorated
  deposit 2_050.00 USD
  from 2026-05-15 until 2027-05-31
  // the journal starts it on its day with `jordan-lee rents unit-c from 2026-05-15`, a verb of the kind

// ── what the kinds above declare (a sketch) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

kind lease : contract
  has tenant    person | org
  has unit      asset
  has landlord  person | org = unit.owner
  has agent     org optional = management[scope unit].manager
  has deposit   amount optional
  covers the month
  input water USD
  also + water * unit.area / unit.whole.area #utilities        // the tenant's share of the building's bill, by area
  also + 5% of rent #late-fees  when date > due + 5d
  law vacancy
    always
    warn any lease where unit is self  "unit has no lease"      // ✗ ll-c02 [A12] needs an existential over the inverse of `unit`
  verb rents ... from                                          // `DATE TENANT rents UNIT from DAY`

// ── the loan, and the rest ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

entity first-federal : lender
  marta/mortgage : loan 374_400.00 USD on 2022-08-12 at 5.25% over 30y for triplex
    monthly on 1 from checking
    also -> escrow 870.00 USD #escrow                          // `escrow` is a position the loan kind implies: marta's, with first-federal
entity flour-city-bank : bank
  marta/checking : deposit
  marta/savings  : deposit
entity rochester-general : employer
entity monroe-county : tax-authority
entity state-farm : insurer
entity national-grid, rochester-water : utility
entity ace-plumbing, ace-painting, floors-plus, northeast-heating : contractor

// ═════ 2025-12-31 ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

opening 2025-12-31
  checking                       14_822.40 USD
  savings                        21_300.00 USD
  first-federal/escrow            5_240.00 USD
  marta/trust                     3_496.00 USD          // December's rents, less 8%: marta's, not yet paid out
  marta/trust                     1_850.00 USD for elena     // the deposits are the tenants'
  marta/trust                     1_950.00 USD for devon
  triplex                          basis 468_000.00 USD since 2022-08-12   // ▸ parts by area: unit-a 168_187.50 · unit-b 153_562.50 · unit-c 146_250.00 · land 62_000.00 in them


2026-01

01 lease-b                                                       // ▸ 1,850.00 USD into marta/trust · - 148.00 USD #management via elm-pm · 1,702.00 is marta's · ⇄ ll-s08 the tenant ledger
01 lease-c                                                       // ▸ 1,950.00 USD into marta/trust · - 156.00 USD #management · 1,794.00 is marta's
01 first-federal/mortgage                                        // ▸ 2,937.45 USD from checking: interest 1,558.29 of triplex · principal 509.16 · escrow 870.00 into first-federal/escrow
                                                             // ▸ the interest is the building's, shared by area: unit-a 560.01 (marta's home, itemized) · unit-b 511.31 · unit-c 486.97 (Schedule E)

10 marta/trust                                                   // ▸ elm-pm pays out 3,496.00 USD to checking: what it held on the 1st, net of its fee · ⇄ ll-s07 its owner statement
                                                             // ✗ ll-c05 [A6] "everything held before the 1st of this month" is a sweep of one position by the acquisition day of its parcels, relative to the day it runs

20 checking -> national-grid 46.30 USD #utilities of triplex

31 first-federal/escrow -> monroe-county 3_920.00 USD #property-tax of triplex   // the January half; shared by area, 35.94% of it is itemized
31 job                                                           // ▸ 4,300.00 USD net pay into checking

31 checking = 19_634.65 USD
31 first-federal/escrow = 2_190.00 USD
31 marta/trust = 7_296.00 USD                                    // ▸ 3,496.00 is marta's, 3,800.00 is held for tenants

2026-02

01 lease-c                                                       // ▸ 1,950.00 · - 156.00
01 first-federal/mortgage                                        // ▸ 2,937.45 USD: interest 1,556.06 · principal 511.39 · escrow 870.00

09 lease-b                                                       // ▸ 1,942.50 USD: 1,850.00 rent + 92.50 late fee (5% after 5 days: due 02-06, paid 02-09) · - 148.00 #management

10 savings -> northeast-heating 11_400.00 USD #improvement of triplex "boiler"   // capital: it joins the building as parts
                                                             // ▸ parts by area: unit-a 4,096.88 (marta's home: basis, never depreciated) · unit-b 3,740.62 · unit-c 3,562.50
                                                             // ▸ each rental part depreciates on its own 27.5 years from February: unit-b 11.34 a month · unit-c 10.80
                                                             // ? ll-u01 [A4] §10 divides a flow of the whole by area; nothing says an improvement of the whole becomes a part of each unit
10 checking -> rochester-water 612.40 USD #utilities of triplex ^water-q4   // the quarterly bill, in marta's name
                                                             // ▸ by area, 1,150 · 1,050 · 1,000 of 3,200 sqft: unit-a 220.08 (hers) · unit-b 200.94 · unit-c 191.38: the last two are claims, billed with March's rent
10 marta/trust                                                   // ▸ elm-pm pays out 3,496.00 USD to checking: what it held on the 1st, net of its fee · ⇄ ll-s07 its owner statement

14 checking -> ace-plumbing 240.00 USD #repair of unit-b "leak under the sink"   // spent: it keeps the unit as it was, so no part

20 checking -> national-grid 48.15 USD #utilities of triplex

28 job

28 checking = 23_592.65 USD
28 first-federal/escrow = 3_060.00 USD
28 marta/trust = 7_388.50 USD                                    // ▸ 3,588.50 is marta's, 3,800.00 is held for tenants

2026-03

01 lease-b                                                       // ▸ 2,050.94 USD: 1,850.00 rent + 200.94 water (1,050 of 3,200 sqft of ^water-q4) · - 148.00 #management
01 lease-c                                                       // ▸ 2,141.38 USD: 1,950.00 rent + 191.38 water · - 156.00 #management
01 first-federal/mortgage                                        // ▸ 2,937.45 USD: interest 1,553.83 · principal 513.62 · escrow 870.00

10 marta/trust                                                   // ▸ elm-pm pays out 3,588.50 USD to checking: what it held on the 1st, net of its fee

20 lease-c ends                                                  // devon leaves nine months early, by agreement
                                                             // ▸ the lease's `covers the month` makes the unused 11 of 31 days of March a claim of devon on marta: 691.94 USD
                                                             // ▸ unit-c has no lease from 03-21. check: `unit-c is vacant`; the forecast carries 0.00 rent for it
                                                             // ✗ ll-c02 [A12] a vacancy is the absence of a lease relator on a rentable unit; v4 has no way to see an absence
20 checking -> national-grid 45.80 USD #utilities of triplex

24 checking -> ace-painting 860.00 USD #repair of unit-c "turnover paint"
24 checking -> floors-plus 1_480.00 USD #improvement of unit-c "new carpet"   // a part of its own: 1,480.00 over 27.5 years, 4.48 a month
                                                             // ? ll-u04 [open] both are under the 2,500.00 per-invoice de minimis safe harbor: the carpet could be expensed. That is an election, and nothing in the language says a choice is made once for a year

31 job

31 checking = 26_157.90 USD
31 first-federal/escrow = 3_930.00 USD
31 marta/trust = 7_688.32 USD                                    // ▸ 3,888.32 is marta's, 3,800.00 is held for tenants

2026-04

01 lease-b                                                       // ▸ 1,850.00 · - 148.00
01 first-federal/mortgage                                        // ▸ 2,937.45 USD: interest 1,551.58 · principal 515.87 · escrow 870.00

03 marta/trust -> devon 1_950.00 USD against ^dep-c              // the deposit, returned on day 14 (NY requires 14)
     - 320.00 USD #cleaning "carpet clean and paint touch-up"    // kept: marta's income, #deposit-retained
     + 691.94 USD #rent "unused 03-21..03-31"                    // the refund of March, owed to him
                                                             // ▸ 2,321.94 USD to devon · the tie on his 1,950.00 is released · ✎ ll-b03 [A3] what an ending lease settles is written by hand here; the lease kind should say it
                                                             // ▸ check: us/ny §7-103 returns within 14 days: kept
// ▸ 04-01 .. 05-14: check says `unit-c vacant 41 days`; the forecast for unit-c is empty

10 marta/trust                                                   // ▸ elm-pm pays out 3,516.38 USD: March's 3,888.32 less devon's 691.94 refund, plus the 320.00 it kept

20 checking -> national-grid 44.20 USD #utilities of triplex

30 job

30 checking = 30_992.63 USD
30 first-federal/escrow = 4_800.00 USD
30 marta/trust = 3_552.00 USD                                    // ▸ 1,702.00 is marta's, 1,850.00 is held for tenants

