// ═════ what Axiom derives ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ▸ axiom flow --by purpose --for marta (rental, H1 2026)                         Schedule E, by unit
//   rent of unit-b   11_100.00 (6 × 1,850.00) + 92.50 late fee · rent of unit-c  6_282.25 (3 × 1,950.00 - 691.94 + 1,124.19)
//   management -1,445.94 (unit-b 888.00 · unit-c 557.94) · leasing -1,025.00 · repair of unit-b -240.00 · repair of unit-c -860.00
//   interest of triplex 9,316.14, of which 5,968.15 is rental (unit-b and unit-c: 64.06% by area) · utilities of the building, by area
//   depreciation unit-b 2,473.17 · unit-c 2,371.10
// ▸ axiom check
//   note[vacant]: unit-c had no lease 03-21..05-14 (55 days); at devon's 1,950.00 a month that is 3,522.59 of rent not collected
//
// ═════ index of marks ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//   ll-b03  ✎     [A3]     an ending lease settles by a rule of its kind: unused prepaid rent, deposit deductions, the 14-day return; written by hand today
//   ll-c02  ✗     [A12]    a vacancy is the absence of a lease relator on a rentable unit: an existential over the inverse of the `unit` slot, and a forecast that knows it
//   ll-c05  ✗     [A6]     the manager pays out "everything held before the 1st of this month": a sweep by acquisition day, relative to the day it runs
//   ll-s07  ⇄     [sync]   the manager's owner statement: one line per unit (a CSV column that is the purpose's object), its fee and the payout, tied to the trust
//   ll-s08  ⇄     [sync]   the tenant ledger (late fee posted, water billed) and the utility PDF that carries the building's area
//   ll-u01  ?     [A4]     an improvement of the whole becomes a part of each unit by area; v4 §10 divides flows of the whole, not capital parts
//   ll-u04  ?     [open]   repair against improvement under the de minimis safe harbor is an election made once a year; nothing says a choice was made
